From: plaz@netcom.com (Geoff Dale)
Date: Fri, 19 Aug 1994 18:40:49 -0700
Subject: [#94-8-226] LEGAL: AnarchyPPL Charter

___________________________________________________________________________

This document is the charter for the AnarchyPPL (PPL-A on HEX). Revision
date: Aug. 19, 1994.

The proprietor of the AnarchyPPL is Geoff Dale, who has taken the title
Anarch. Anarch seems to be a perfect choice for a person who wishes to rule
as little as possible.

AnarchyPPL (PPL-A) Protections:
-------------------------------
First and foremost, PPL-A commits to do what a PPL is supposed to do,
protect its members. It will protect them from arbitrary judgments of other
PPLs and the effects of tempers of list members. The PPL will go to bat for
them as long as they stay within it's rules. The ExI-Board still has the
right to expel a person from the list, but the PPL promises to be it's
clients' advocate in that forum as well.

The PPL may look into being a mutual protection society. If it is felt that
unjust charges or actions are brought against its members, alternatives
will be discussed on how to use the membership (on a voluntary basis of
course) to redress the issue.

AnarchyPPL (PPL-A) Rules:
-------------------------
In accordance with the principles of anarchy and spontaneous order, this
PPL's rules are kept down to minimal levels, and netiquette is not
enforced. Politeness will grow from social interactions or the individual
will find himself ::excluded by just about everyone. The marketable
attribute of having something to say will counteract this effect on certain
individuals, but this is desirable as well.

Serious Offenses:
1> Spoofing, fraud, and libel.

2> Forwarding list messages to a third party (defined as a party not
either subscribed to the list, or a member ExI) without the author(s)
permission.

3> In addition, having a formal complaint being made on a person for
excessive and repeated rudeness by a member of Anarchy-PPL or any other
PPL.

The Anarch will consider ejecting (from the PPL) or banning (from posting
for a period of time) any person who is accused of committing a serious
offense on a case-by-case basis, but never before cautioning the person
that he/she is treading the line and giving him/her the chance to change
his/her tune. If the person is deemed to have committed the offense and it
is deemed necessary by the Anarch, the offender must post a retraction or
apology for the said offense. Failure to do so will result in expulsion
from the PPL.

If a member is ejected from the Anarchy PPL and no other PPL will take
him/her in, that member is effectively kicked off the list. Harry has made
it clear that you must belong to some PPL.

Minor Offenses:
1> The omission of the mandatory META, FORWARD/FWD, POLL, and PLEDGE
prefixes, on messages that should have used them.

        META - List specific business. Software change suggestions, policy
                questions, etc.
        FWD - All postings that did not appear here on this list first.
        POLL - Any polls of list members, or results from polls.
        PLEDGE - Pledge drives.
        LEGAL - PPL business.

2> Arguing against the basics, as strictly defined as:

        A> Statist arguments
                Intermediate strategies explicitly excepted.

        B> Deathist arguments
                Strictly defined as pro-death, anti-life extension.
                NOT as anything Reilly Jones classifies as
                death-worshipping entropism.

        C> Religion-ist arguments
                Rational discussion of religious philosophies
                explicitly excepted. Just don't push the faith, or
                existence of gods, aspects. No flying yogis.

Minor offenders will be issued warnings until the point were it becomes a
serious offense type 3 (meaning: until someone brings a formal complaint).
Warnings previously issued may be considered the members "chance to change
his/her tune" at the Anarch's discretion.

AnarchyPPL (PPL-A)
A Summary of what is allowed but wasn't allowed in PPL-1:
---------------------------------------------------------

Public plonkings, setting the facts straight, and defending one's honor
will explicitly be permitted. These, as a matter of fact, happen all the
time in PPL-1 with no one batting an eye. Judiciously used, these can act
as a powerful social feedback mechanism.

I personally still think that ad hominem attacks and me-too messages are
bad things. I just don't think "there ought to be a law" to protect us from
them. People can protect themselves from this. This fine list software we
now have especially empowers people to ::exclude idiots, and people who
offend them.

Sending someone feedback (negative or positive) via private e-mail is
highly recommended.

Note that the "third party" has been defined as "a party not either
subscribed to the list, or a member ExI," for the purposes of forwarding
list traffic without the permission of the author(s).

AnarchyPPL (PPL-A) How to join:
---------------------------------------
If you are interested in joining PPL-A, send private e-mail me at
plaz@netcom.com and you should also notify your current PPL provider that
you are intending to leave hir PPL. State that you want to join the
AnarchyPPL (or PPL-A) and quit PPL-1.

Joining the PPL is considered to be a contract to agree by its rules.

The AnarchyPPL was accepted by Harry Shapiro as a legal PPL for the
extropians list on the 30th Dec., 1993. On this date, Aug. 19, 1994, it has
